    <!-- XFTL's own nebulas, see doc/game/nebulas.md -->
    <text name="xftl_big_ship_salvage">The rest of the bigger ship's wreckage has more to salvage.</text>
    <text name="xftl_sector_legend_hazard">Hazardous</text>
    <text name="xftl_sector_hazard">Unidentified Hazardous Sector</text>
    <text name="xftl_sensors_nebula">Blocked by the nebula: your sensors don't work here.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_extreme_loc">EXTREME HAZARD: two hazards at once.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_catastrophic_loc">CATASTROPHIC HAZARD: three hazards at once.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_apocalyptic_loc">APOCALYPTIC HAZARD: a nebula, asteroids, a sun and a pulsar, all at once.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_radiation_loc">Radiation Nebula. The radiation here will slowly hurt any crew outside the medbay or clonebay, and disrupt your sensors.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_mirage_loc">Mirage Nebula. Sensor ghosts here make your map unreliable: ships and hazards may not be what they seem.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_dark_loc">Dark Nebula. Nothing gets through this nebula: your sensors and drones won't work here.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_mirage_confused">Your sensors are confused by the mirage nebula. This may not be accurate.</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_chorus_loc">Chorus-held. CONCORD's signal is so strong here that your sensors show what it wants them to: ships and hazards may not be what they seem.</text>
    <text name="xftl_warning_radiation">RADIATION NEBULA</text>
    <text name="xftl_warning_mirage">MIRAGE\nVISION IS UNRELIABLE</text>
    <text name="xftl_warning_dark">DARKNESS\nDRONES OFFLINE</text>
    <text name="xftl_map_boss_loc">The sector's boss holds the exit: you can't leave the sector until it's beaten.</text>
    <text name="xftl_zoltan_shield_boarded">Your boarders have taken two ships with Zoltan shields. Your engineers strip the better of the two shield generators, and wire it into your own ship.</text>
    <text name="xftl_exit_hold_broken">With the command ship gone, the blockade falls apart, and the Rebel fleet behind you surges forward to close the gap. Its ships are already at the line's other exits. There's only one way left: onwards, out of the sector.</text>
